ified that i might be a bit too old  for this  it's it gets harder and harder to to  deal with that number four this scene  was happy tears who didn't get choked up  at the end of no way home when all the  spider-man said their final goodbyes tom  holland andrew garfield and toby mcguire  all loved the time they spent together  on set and it felt like a dream come  true for all of them the hug they all  shared was actually written into the  script after the director and writers  saw the three actors embrace and start  crying together on their own it was the  perfect way to show how much the  spider-man meant to each other both in  the film and in real life yep that's how  we're gonna end the film  number five the redemption is real  andrew garfield's peter catching  zendaya's mj was an incredible moment  full of raw emotions and that wasn't  lost on the two actors they had an  amazing time shooting the scene and it  was actually the first thing the two  shot together i met you yesterday thanks  for catching me how are you you good  okay you have to cry sorry it was a  scene that completed an arc started  seven years ago during the amazing  spider-man 2 and it was a cathartic  experience for both the audience and the  actors it's pretty intense it went like  that and then suddenly we were kind of  done number six is this the end tom  zendaya and jacob all cried together  after filming their last scene of no way  home because it felt like it could be  the last time all three of them would be  together for the spider-man films we  were definitely treating no way home  like it was coming to an end and it felt  like it in a way it is like things are  coming to an end as director john watts  explained that no way home was the last  movie in the homecoming trilogy and that  the next story would be very different  it would be heartbreaking if we never  got to see these three together again it  was heartbreaking but also really  exciting because we're all moving into  the next chapter of our careers i don't  think i've cried like that ever  so it's been incredible it's been  honestly the best thing that's ever  happened to me number seven this may be  the saddest scene in spider-man history  aunt may's passing was a huge emotional  plot point in no way home and it was  very emotional to film tom holland felt  a special connection between his  character and mate the relationship  between me and marissa throughout these  films has been really integral to the  heart and soul of the story not only did  we have to say goodbye to aunt may but  it was also a goodbye to marissa tomei  who means so much to everyone who worked  on the movies shout out to aunt may  number eight mr stark none of us feel  good after this scene tom holland's  infamous i don't wanna go scene in  infinity war was actually improvised by  holland tom has a specific routine he  does before he needs to shoot an  emotional crying scene he repeats a word  or phrase over and over again until he  becomes emotional in this case it was  the i don't want to go line which is why  it feels so real and visceral on screen  i don't want to go you don't want to go  please we had so much fun on those sets  but when we got into the emotion of that  moment we really dived into it  number nine we love these three together  andrew garfield got emotional on the set  of no way home simply because he got to  be on set with tom holland and toby  maguire far too old to be playing  spider-man now but they they asked me  back the sweetest thing ever he loved  the role he played in the movie acting  as an older brother mentor figure to the  younger tom holland spider-man while  also being a younger brother in awe of  toby maguire's older spidey the three  worked incredibly well together and  their love for each other was very real  we can't imagine anyone else in these  roles we kind of feel things in each  other we challenge things in each other  number ten this one is all about  positive emotion